      "id": 171721,
      "name": "aawood",
      "username": "aawood",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/8e8cbc/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2016-04-06T11:33:15.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I'm just picturing two people sat in the same room, playing the game on tablets. The Guise player is sweating.</p><p>\"I have to\", they say.</p><p>\"Don't you da...\" The other player doesn't get a chance to finish, as the first taps to play \"I'm that guy\". They lock eyes. There is anger there, perhaps. Resignation, certainly.</p><p>They stand, facing each other, each balancing their tablet on the palm of their right hand. No words are needed. They know what must happen. On a nod, they scream in unison, flinging their hands up and forwards, tablets first, to meet in mid-air in a shower of glass and electronics and rage.</p><p>In hindsight, they decide this was not the best play for turn 1.</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:54:29.037Z",
